%I A397756 #30 Aug 17 2026 17:24:56
%S A397756 21,41,51,86,201,251,281,401,501,651,801,926,1701,2001,2501,3141,3701,
%T A397756 3801,4001,5001,8001,8121,11501,12501,14801,19781,20001,20781,22601,
%U A397756 23751,25001,26001,28901,29001,31001,40001,49001,49761,50001,71841,72501,80001
%N A397756 Numbers i and j both with m digits such that i*j = 10^m*R(i) + j, where R(x) is the digit reversal of x; j may end in 0.
%C A397756 Read as an irregular triangle: row m lists the terms having m digits, m >= 2,in increasing order. Row lengths are 4, 8, 10, 20, 22, 35, 45, 58 for m = 2..9.
%C A397756 The corresponding products i*j are in A398801, whose rows have the same lengths but are in increasing order of i*j = 10^m*R(i) + j, that is, of R(i); the two orders coincide only for m = 2.
%C A397756 Equivalently, i-1 divides 10^m*R(i) and the quotient j has m digits.
%C A397756 If c divides 10^m and 2 <= c <= 9, then i = c*10^(m-1)+1 is a term, with j = 10^m/c + 10. In base 10 this gives four infinite families, c = 2, 4, 5 and 8, the last one from m >= 3 on.
%C A397756 Terms outside these families exist, the smallest being 86, with j = 80.
%C A397756 The products i*j form a subset of A014575.
%H A397756 Gnouma Jerome Kadouno, <a href="/A397756/b397756.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..202</a>
%H A397756 G. J. Kadouno, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21820428">Janus numbers: classification and infinite families</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A397756 D. Potapov, <a href="https://habr.com/ru/articles/795935/">Numbers that flip on multiplication</a>, Habr, 2024 (in Russian).
%e A397756 21 is a term: 21*60 = 1260, the concatenation of R(21) = 12 and 60.
%e A397756 86 is a term: 86*80 = 6880, the concatenation of R(86) = 68 and 80.
%e A397756 2001 is a term: 2001*5010 = 10025010, the concatenation of R(2001) = 1002 and 5010.
%o A397756 (Python)
%o A397756 def agen():
%o A397756     m = 2
%o A397756     while True:
%o A397756         M = 10**m
%o A397756         for i in range(M//10, M):
%o A397756             R = int(str(i)[::-1])
%o A397756             if (M*R) % (i-1) == 0:
%o A397756                 j = M*R // (i-1)
%o A397756                 if M//10 <= j < M: yield i
%o A397756         m += 1
%o A397756 A397756 = agen()
%o A397756 print([next(A397756) for i in range(42)])
%o A397756 (PARI) row(n) = my(list=List()); for (i=10^(n-1), 10^n-1, my(R = fromdigits(Vecrev(digits(i)))); for (j=10^(n-1), 10^n-1, if (i*j == 10^n*R + j, listput(list, i)););); Vec(list); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Aug 10 2026
%Y A397756 Cf. A014575, A009944, A398801, A048935.
